// mlrepro (2026-07-17, v-compiler-ml) — FOLLOW-UP to the memoized-query-DB effect friction v-effects fixed
// in 4a8b278b6. The fix genuinely advanced the boundary (put;get in ONE sequence folds; put;get-via-a-helper
// folds). But a NARROWER shape remains, and it now manifests as a WRONG VALUE (silent), not a clean decline:
//
//   A HELPER that performs BOTH get AND put internally (the memoize combinator: `get k; on miss put k v`)
//   does NOT propagate its out-state to a LATER perform in the CALLER's sequence.
//
// PINNED bisection (all under the SAME two-op Map-state handler):
//   - demand(5, 25) ALONE                                  → 25   ✓ (single call, internal get-miss then put)
//   - Db.put((1,42)) ; Db.get(1)          (inline seq)     → 42   ✓ (v-effects' verified repro)
//   - Db.put((1,42)) ; lookup-or(1, -1)   (get via helper) → 42   ✓
//   - let a = demand(5,25) in Db.get(5)   (put INSIDE the first helper, get after)  → None ✗  EXPECTED Some 25
//
// So: a `put` performed INSIDE a helper is invisible to a `get` performed AFTER that helper returns, in the
// caller's sequence. The helper's out-state is dropped at the return boundary. This is the load-bearing
// memoized-DB shape (producer fills its column, a later producer/read sees the fill), so effect-Db (design A)
// still can't express the lazy query DB; the port stays on the PURE THREADED-DB (design B, db.cdz — works).
//
// ⚠ SEVERITY NOTE: unlike the original (clean decline), this COMPILES + RUNS to a WRONG VALUE (the memo silently
// misses). A silent wrong result is worse than a decline — flagging in case the fold should DECLINE this shape
// until it can thread the helper out-state, rather than emit a lossy memo.
//
// EXPECTED: run-then-get() == 50 (demand fills 5→25, the later get(5) sees Some 25, 25 + 25 = 50).
// ACTUAL:   run-then-get() returns -1 (the get(5) MISSES — demand's internal put was lost).

effect Db =
  | get : Int64 -> Option(Int64)
  | put : Tuple(Int64, Int64) -> Unit

// the memoize combinator: get; on a miss, put then return the computed value.
def demand(k: Int64, compute: Int64) =
  (match Db.get(k) with
    | Option.Some(v) => v
    | Option.None(_) => (Db.put((k, compute)); compute))

def run-then-get() =
  handle Db(Map.empty) with
    | get(k, s) => resume(Map.lookup(s, k), s)
    | put(kv, s) => (match kv with | (k, v) => resume(unit, Map.insert(s, k, v)))
  in
  (let a = demand(5, 25) in (match Db.get(5) with | Option.Some(v) => a + v | Option.None(_) => 0 - 1))

@test
def effect-db-helper-outstate-lost() =
  if run-then-get() == 50 then unit else trap("demand's internal put should be visible to a later get: 25+25=50")

export { run-then-get }
